Comment: The application is linked against the LVGL based cp0_lvgl runtime of the
 CardputerZero launcher by M5Stack (Copyright M5Stack Technology CO LTD, MIT) and LVGL
 (Copyright LVGL Kft, MIT), which are part of the binary and are therefore listed in
 its Copyright field below. The fonts it draws with are the launcher's, read at run
 time from /usr/share/APPLaunch/share/font (Montserrat: SIL OFL 1.1; JetBrains Mono:
 SIL OFL 1.1); none is shipped in this package. One font IS part of the binary: Caveat
 SemiBold (SIL OFL 1.1), the handwriting of the cassette label, compiled in as LVGL
 bitmap fonts (ASCII and Latin-1 at four sizes, generated from the pinned
 googlefonts/caveat sources, commit 59745e8; the instance at weight 600 was cut from
 the variable font with fontTools). The font's own copyright line and licence are
 below; its copyright holder declares no Reserved Font Name.
 .
 The capture and playback layer, the ring buffer, the WAV / Broadcast Wave / RF64
 writer, the journal and the repair step, the meter and the gain, the trim and split
 editor, the take list, the settings and the screens are the app's own code, written
 from scratch for this project from the published file format documents (EBU Tech 3285
 Broadcast Wave, EBU Tech 3306 RF64) and the ALSA library's API documentation. The
 package holds no code of other recorder programs.
 .
 Sound cards are reached through the ALSA library, libasound.so.2 of the system
 (alsa-lib, LGPL-2.1-or-later), opened at run time: it is neither linked into the
 binaries nor shipped in this package (the package depends on libasound2t64 or
 libasound2 so that apt installs it).
 .
 usr/share/APPLaunch/bin/cassette-probe is a small listen-only command line tool built
 from the same capture layer (it lists the sound cards and their controls and opens
 each card for two seconds to count frames, writing no file and changing no setting),
 for the board tests.

